# SECOND SECTION: kagent 0.10 (dev/kagent/up-0.10.sh; KAGENT_VERSION=0.10 of dev/kagent-e2e.sh). Read by the same `pin()`: its keys start with `kagent010_`.
# The node image (`kind_node_image`), the bundled Postgres' and WireMock's digests above are shared.
#
# kagent v0.10.3 (2026-09-28) is the newest 0.10. It runs a declarative agent as an ordinary Deployment of its own runtime image (Go ADK `golang-adk`, or
# Python `app`), NOT as an Actor of Agent Substrate: the chart's `substrate.enabled` and `substrateWorkerPool.create` are false (Substrate is there for the
# sandboxed agents of the OpenClaw harness only), so this scenario installs no Substrate, sets no feature gate and needs no gVisor: a plain kind node.
# It serves the A2A v1 wire at /api/a2a/{namespace}/{name}, beside the legacy one, chosen by the `A2A-Version` header (missing or 0.3: legacy, 1.0: v1);
# the orchestrator's client sends 1.0 on every call.
#
# VERIFIED 2026-10-07 by READING kagent at v0.10.3 (raw files of https://github.com/kagent-dev/kagent/tree/v0.10.3) and the anonymous registry API. None
# of it has been RUN by us: the first run of the `kagent-010` job of .github/workflows/kagent-e2e.yml is the proof or the disproof.
#   * helm/kagent/values.yaml: `substrate.enabled: false`, `substrateWorkerPool.create: false`, `controller.agentDeployment` ("Global deployment defaults applied
#     to all agent pods"), `controller.goAgentImage.repository: kagent-dev/kagent/golang-adk`, `controller.a2aBaseUrl` ("The base URL of the A2A Server endpoint, as
#     advertised to clients"), `controller.auth.mode: unsecure` (default: the X-User-Id header, else admin@kagent.dev), `ui.replicas`, and the built-in agents
#     (k8s-agent ... cilium-debug-agent), `kagent-tools`, `grafana-mcp` and `kmcp`, which are ON by default (the values of this scenario turn them off)
#   * go/core/internal/httpserver/server.go: the route `/api/a2a/{namespace}/{name}`; go/core/internal/utils/a2a_version.go: the `A2A-Version` header
#   * go/api/v1alpha2: group `kagent.dev`, version `v1alpha2`; `AgentSpec.type` (Declarative), `declarative.{runtime, systemMessage, modelConfig, stream}`;
#     `ModelConfig.spec.{model, provider, apiKeySecret, apiKeySecretKey, openAI.baseUrl}`
#   * go/core/test/e2e/invoke_api_test.go: the card is `<controller>/api/a2a/<ns>/<name>/.well-known/agent-card.json`, and kagent's own end-to-end tests create a
#     ModelConfig and a declarative Agent in namespace `kagent` and wait for `agents.kagent.dev` to be `Ready`
#   * go/core/internal/controller/translator/agent/deployments.go: a regular declarative agent is given the TAG reference of the runtime image, and a tag with an
#     embedded digest is used as it is (only the `-full` variant needs `fullDigest`; an agent without skills or a sandbox is not one)
#   * charts: oci://ghcr.io/kagent-dev/kagent/helm/kagent-crds and .../kagent, version 0.10.3; the digest is the Docker-Content-Digest of the tag (what `helm pull` prints)
#
# The images the chart runs (digest = the image INDEX of the tag; the controller and the Go runtime are pinned in kagent-values-0.10.yaml, the rest are not used):
#   ghcr.io/kagent-dev/kagent/controller:0.10.3  index sha256:b2572a59386b6bac1f5e652e135fdad54c0ee603d3f9ee60eb7c80bbaedf9b76
#   ghcr.io/kagent-dev/kagent/golang-adk:0.10.3  index sha256:5ee9592cb7d959538d0f0fe36acf31ba3a06de084f84048b1459c3bdfafcda1f  (the agent's runtime, `declarative.runtime: go`)
